cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use VeriSCS, please cite it using this metadata.
title: "VeriSCS: an executable reference for a machine-checked factor-2 shortest common superstring"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kern
    given-names: Konrad
    alias: buberlo
repository-code: "https://github.com/buberlo/veriscs"
url: "https://github.com/buberlo/veriscs"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
abstract: >-
  VeriSCS runs the Lean function OAI.Superstring.answer from the public
  openai/math repository and prints a common superstring. The vendored proof
  states that the result is a common superstring of length at most twice the
  optimum and that the function has a polynomial-time Turing-machine
  implementation. The native binary, the text codec, and the Python checker
  are outside that proof.
